faceid-nim (1.1.0-1) noble; urgency=high

  * FIX: the vision worker could not start at all. models.py had a
    one-character syntax error ("license: str,") that made
    build_engine() -- the function that constructs the whole worker --
    unimportable. No test imported that module, so the suite stayed green
    while nothing could run. vision/tests/test_imports.py now compiles and
    imports every module, including a CI job that builds the packaged venv
    exactly as debian/rules does and imports all of it.

  * FIX: MediaPipe Face Mesh was never running. The worker asked for
    mp.solutions.face_mesh, an API the installed wheel (0.10.x) no longer
    ships, and the resulting AttributeError was swallowed into a silent
    "unavailable". Blink, parallax, challenge-response and the attention
    check were therefore inert no-ops in a shipped build, and
    strictness = heavy could never be satisfied. landmarks.py is now a
    backend registry that prefers the supported MediaPipe Tasks API, and
    every failure carries a reason that reaches `faceid-nim status` and
    the app instead of being swallowed.

  * Dense landmarks are now provisioned automatically. face_landmarker.task
    is pinned by SHA-256 in the manifest and fetched by fetch-models. The
    manifest gains an `optional` key: absent is a degraded feature that is
    reported, not a silent no-op. The detector and the recogniser stay
    required, so a machine missing either still fails loudly.

  * The passive ML anti-spoof model is still not fetchable (no published
    ONNX export at a stable URL). It is now unpinned AND optional, so it
    is refused rather than half-loaded, and every user-facing surface says
    the check is unavailable instead of implying it runs.

  * Installing the package now actually provisions it. postinst fetches
    the models (non-fatal; a new faceid-nim-fetch-models.service retries
    on every boot for a machine that was offline), detects the colour and
    infrared cameras into the generated config, and prints the state it
    achieved rather than a list of commands to type. postrm stops the
    units and removes the generated GPU drop-in.

  * `faceid-nim status` reports what is ACTUALLY running -- the live
    landmark backend, the anti-spoof state, the execution provider and
    thread count, the loaded model -- not just what is installed. The app
    shows the same and warns when liveness is reduced.

  * Inference is provisioned for the machine instead of hard-coded. A new
    hardware probe (vision/faceid_vision/hardware.py) picks an execution
    provider by constructing a real session and checking what came back --
    onnxruntime downgrades to CPU with only a log line, so its provider
    list is not evidence -- and sizes threads from the cgroup/affinity
    limit rather than the host core count. A new gpu-devices script widens
    the worker's systemd sandbox only when a GPU is actually present. The
    recogniser and the anti-spoof model now share one session factory and
    can no longer drift apart.

  * arm64 is buildable. mediapipe publishes no arm64 wheel, which made the
    liveness extra a hard build failure and therefore no package at all
    for every ARM laptop. The extra is now best-effort per architecture,
    with a venv import check after it, and the app reports the reduced
    liveness honestly. CI builds the .deb for both amd64 and arm64.

  * opencv is pinned below 5 and to the headless distribution; the
    declared dependency was being satisfied by opencv-contrib-python,
    which pulls GUI libraries into a headless system service.

  * Camera discovery moved to vision/faceid_vision/cameras.py so
    postinst, the CLI and the app all use one implementation, with the app
    re-exporting it. Fresh installs get auto-detected cameras and
    mode = "auto" (dark room -> IR, lit room -> RGB).

  * packaging/scripts/install.sh picks the .deb matching
    dpkg --print-architecture and refuses a mismatched package.

  * Documentation corrections: polkit IS wired (architecture.md said it
    was not), the worker socket path was wrong, matcher.rs's comment
    claimed the best score reaches the audit log (it does not), and the
    preview pipe framing description omitted its 'J'/'G' tag byte.
    emitter_difference() is now explicitly documented as not wired into
    any scan, and is unit-tested as a result.

 -- Gaurav <gaurav@example.invalid>  Sat, 26 Sep 2026 16:30:00 +0540

faceid-nim (1.0.2-1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Package the settings-app launcher (/usr/bin/faceid-app) which the
    desktop entry runs; a fresh install previously shipped no app
    binary at all.
  * Camera discovery: a mono-only capture node with real frame sizes is
    a genuine IR sensor (combo RGB+IR webcams share one UVC card name);
    it is no longer demoted to an RGB alternate, so IR and Hybrid modes
    work on such machines.
  * The app exposes the full camera-mode set again: Automatic, RGB,
    IR and Hybrid (RGB + IR, daemon mode "both"). Hybrid falls back to
    RGB with a note when no IR sensor exists.

 -- Gaurav <gaurav@example.invalid>  Mon, 21 Sep 2026 22:30:00 +0545

faceid-nim (1.0.1-1) noble; urgency=medium

  * verify-models / fetch-models: unpinned manifest entries (the
    optional MiniFASNet anti-spoof model has a placeholder hash by
    design) are now treated as optional and skipped instead of failing.
    A clean install no longer prints a false "models missing or
    unverified" banner on machines that legitimately ship without that
    model.

